ther a one-time gardener for  uk forces in afghanistan who's still  stranded there  he said the taliban came into the  village because the taliban's everywhere  now in in afghanistan  he said to me i don't trust anymore i  don't i don't trust anymore just you i  mean i don't trust the the the  government the uk government because he  said  they they they have promised me so many  times but to look at that i'm still left  behind  for the special forces as well as fear  of capture many no longer have a job and  money is running short  it means time is running out for the uk  to make good on its word to rescue its  friends  debra haynes sky news
 

